\[ \text{Base Area} = \text{Weight} \times 0.0333 \]  
First, we need to convert the weight from lbs to lb.  
The weight of the person is 65 lb.  
The height of the person is 3 ft 6 in.  
First, convert the height to feet:  
\[ 3 \text{ ft} + 6 \text{ in} = 3 \text{ ft} + \frac{6}{12} \text{ ft} = 3 + 0.5 = 3.5 \text{ ft} \]  
Next, calculate the base area:  
\[ \text{Base Area} = 65 \text{ lb} \times 0.0333 = 2.16 \text{ m}^2 \]  
Now, multiply the base area by the dosage rate:  
\[ \text{Delivery} = 2.16 \times 17.5 = 37.2 \text{ mg} \]  
Thus, the required dosage is \(\boxed{37.2 \text{ mg}}\).  

