- The concentration of B₂ is the same (\([B_2] = 1.00 \, \text{M}\))
- The concentration of A is doubled (\([A]\) increases from 0.50 M to 1.00 M)
- The rate remains the same (\([R] = 3.2 \times 10^{-4} \, \text{Ms}^{-1}\))

Since doubling the concentration of A does not change the rate, the order of the reaction with respect to A is 0.

\[
\text{Rate} = k [A]^0 [B_2]^1
