ΔHf[Fe(H₂O)6]²⁺ = ΔHhydration[Fe(H₂O)6]²⁺ = -340 kJ/mol

Now, we can calculate the standard enthalpy change for the reaction:

ΔH = ΔHf[FeCl₄]²⁻ - [ΔHf[Fe(H₂O)₆]²⁺ + 2ΔHhydration(Cl⁻)]
ΔH = -392 kJ/mol - [0 + 2(-381) kJ/mol]
ΔH = -392 kJ/mol - (-762 kJ/mol)
ΔH = -392 kJ/mol + 762 kJ/mol
ΔH = 370 kJ/mol

