","The system reliability function \( R_S(t) \) is the probability that the system fails after time \( t \). For a non-resistant system, the system fails if all components fail.  

1. A **Serial System**:  
   In a serial system, the system fails if and only if all components fail. If the components are \( n \) independent components with reliability functions \( R_1(t), R_2(t), R_3(t), \ldots, R_n(t) \), the system reliability function is the product of the individual reliability functions:  
   \[
   R_S(t) = R_1(t) \cdot R_2(t) \cdot R_3(t) \cdot \cdots \ \cdots R_n(t) = \prod_{i=1}^n R_i(t)
   \]  
   This means the system is reliable if and only if all components are reliable.  

2. **Parallel System**:  
   In a parallel system, the system is reliable if only only if only least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least least:  
