\[ 2 \text{PbS(s)} [91.2] + 3 \text{O}_2(g) [205.1] \rightarrow 2 \text{PbO(s)} [66.5] + 2 \text{SO}_2(g) [248.2] \]
</USER_REQUEST>

<ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>
The entropy change (ΔS) for the reaction is calculated as follows:

\[
\Delta S = \sum \Delta S^\circ (\text{products}) - \sum \Delta S^\circ (\text{reactants})
\]

Substituting the given molar entropies:

\[
\Delta S = (2 \times 66.5) + (2 \times 248.2) - (2 \times 91.2) - (3 \times 205.1)
\]

\[
\Delta S = 133 + 496.4 - 182.4 - 615.3
\]

\[
\Delta S = 629.4 - 797.7
\]

\[
\Delta S = -168.3 \text{ J/K mol}
\]

Thus, the entropy change is \(\boxed{-168.3 \text{ J/K mol}}\).
