In a dimerization process where a partially resolved chiral substrate reacts to form homochiral (\( RR \) or \( SS \)) and meso (\( RS \) or \( SR \)) dimers, how does the selectivity factor \( s = k_e / k_m \) (where \( k_e \) is the rate constant for homochiral dimer formation and \( k_m \) is the rate constant for meso dimer formation) affect the amplification of the enantiomeric excess (e.e.) of the optically active substance?<end_of_turn>
