\]
Since \( \tan^{-1}(x) \) is a continuous function, we can evaluate the limit as:
\[
\lim_{h \to 0} \tan^{-1}\left(\frac{1}{h}\right) = \tan^{-1}\left(\lim_{h \to 0} \frac{1}{h}\right).
\]
