3. **Time to catch up**:  
   b needs to cover 30 km to catch up to a, and they approach each another at a relative speed of 10 kmph, so b takes 30 km / 10 kmph = 3 hours to catch up.

4. **Distance from start**:  
   Since b starts after 3 hours, b catches up to a after 3 hours (after starting b). Therefore, b catches up to a at 20 kmph × 3 h = 60 km from the start.

