     \[
     \text{Re} = \frac{\rho u L}{\mu} \implies u = \frac{\rho \text{Re L}}{\mu}
     \]  
     For air at 500°C, \( \rho = 1.016 \, \text{kg/m}^3 \) and \( \mu = 0.000101 \, \text{kg/m s} \).  
     \[
     u = \frac{1.016 \times 40,000 \times 0.2}{0.000101} = 8.01 \, \text{m/s}
     \]  

   - **Nusselt Number**:  
     For fully turbulent flow (which is the case here, \( \text{Re} > 10,000 \)), the Blasius chart or Moody chart can be used to estimate the Nusselt number.  
     \[
     Nu = 0.000000012 \times \text{Re}^3.5 \times Pr^{0.25}
     \]  
     For air at 500°C, \( \text{Pr} = 0.0006 \).  
     \[
     Nu = 0.000000012 \times 40,000^{3.5} \times 0.0006 = 1.009 \times 10^5
     \]  

