- \(V_{BS}\) is the base-tosource voltage.
- \(\phi_s\) is the built-work function of the substrate.
- \(\phi_b\) is the built-work function of the base.
- \(q\) is the elementary charge (\(1.6 \times 10^{-19} \text{ C}\)).
- \(k\) is the Boltzmann constant (\(1.38 \times 10^{-23} \text{ J/K}\)).
- \(T\) is the temperature in Kelvin.

For a p-channel MOSFET, the threshold voltage is given by:

\[
V_{T} = \frac{1}{2} V_{BS} - \frac{1}{2} V_{BS(0)}
\]

where \(V_{BS(0)}\) is the built-up voltage at \(V_{BS} = 0\).

The built-up voltage is given by:

\[
V_{BS(0)} = \frac{q \phi_s}{q_i}
\]

