","To calculate the recoil velocity of the Earth, we use the principle of momentum conservation. The total momentum of the system (cannonball + Earth) must be zero initially (since the system is initially at rest). After the cannonball is fired, the momentum of the system must also be zero.

1. **Initial Momentum:**
   \[
   m_{\text{ball}} v_{\text{ball}} + m_{\text{earth}} v_{\text{earth}} = 0
   \]
   Since the Earth is initially at rest, \(v_{\text{earth}} = 0\). Thus, the initial momentum is zero.

2. **Final Momentum:**
   \[
   m_{\text{ball}} v_{\text{ball,final}} + m_{\text{earth}} v_{\text{earth,final}} = 0
   \]
   Substituting the given values:
   \[
   (1 \, \text{kg})(90.0 \, \text{m/s}) + (5.97 \times 10^{24} \, \text{kg}) v_{\text{earth,final}} = 0
   \]
   Solving for \(v_{\text{earth,final}}\):
   \[
   v_{\text{earth,final}} = \frac{-(1 \, \text{kg})(90.0 \, \text{m/s})}{5.97 \times 10^{24} \, \text{kg}}
   \]
   \[
   v_{\text{earth,final}} = \frac{-90.0}{5.97 \times 10^{24}} \, \text{m/s}
   \]
   \[
   v_{\text{earth,final}} = -1.52 \times 10^{-22} \, \text{m/s}
   \]

The recoil velocity of the Earth is \(\boxed{-1.52 \times 10^{-22} \, \text{m/s}}\). The negative sign indicates the direction of the recoil is opposite to the cannonball's motion.",fluency,"# Task Description
