<ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>
The curl of a vector field \(\mathbf{V}(x, y) = \mathbf{i} V_x(x, y) + \mathbf{j} V_y(x, y)\) is given by:
\[
\nabla \times \mathbf{V} = \frac{\partial}{\partial y} V_x - \frac{\partial}{\partial x} V_y
\]
Thus, the curl of \(\mathbf{V}(x, y)\) is:
\[
\nabla \times \mathbf{V} = \left( \frac{\partial}{\partial y} V_x(x, y) \right) \mathbf{i} - \left( \frac{\partial}{\partial x} V_y(x, y) \right) \mathbf{j}
\]

The curl of \(\mathbf{V}(x, y)\) is a vector with components:
\[
\boxed{\left( \frac{\partial}{\partial y} V_x, -\frac{\partial}{\partial x} V_y, 0 \right)}
\]
