For the Σ⁺ meson, the rest energy \( E_0 = 1385 \text{ MeV} \) and the lifetime \( \Delta t = 2.0 \times 10^{-23} \text{ s} \). The energy spread \( \Delta E \) is given by:  
\[
\Delta E \geq \frac{\hbar}{\Delta t}
\]  
The reduced Planck constant is \( \hbar = 1.054 \times 10^{-34} \text{ J s} \).  
First, convert the lifetime to seconds:  
\[
\Delta t = 2.0 \times 10^{-23} \text{ s}
\]  
Now, compute \( \Delta E \):  
\[
\Delta E \geq \frac{1.054 \times 10^{-34} \text{ J s}}{2.0 \times 10^{-23} \text{ s}} = 5.27 \times 10^{-12} \text{ J}
\]  
