","The covariant derivative of a vector \( V^\mu \) in curved spacetime is given by:
\[
\nabla V^\mu = \frac{\partial V^\mu}{\partial \tau} + g^{\mu\nu} \Gamma_{\mu\nu} V^\mu,
\]
where:
- \( \nabla V^\mu \) is the covariant derivative of the vector \( V^\mu \).
- \( \frac{\partial V^\mu}{\partial \tau} \) is the four-velocity of the vector \( V^\mu \), where \( \tau \) is the proper time.
