2 atm * 4 L = 2 moles * 0.0821 L atm / (mol K) * T

8 L atm = 0.1642 L atm / K * T

T = 48.74 K

Now we can calculate the work done during the isothermal expansion:

W = nRT * ln(Vf / Vi)

W = 2 moles * 0.0821 L atm / (mol K) * 48.74 K * ln(8 L / 4 L)

W = 2 * 0.0821 * 48.74 * ln(2)

W = 8.0084 * ln(2)

W ≈ 5.54 L atm

